          "filename": "Ruined Building on Pabbay, Outer Hebrides - geograph.org.uk - 91358.jpg",
          "caption": "Ruined Building on Pabbay, Outer Hebrides. This photo shows a ruined building on Pabbay, an island near Mingulay in the Outer Hebrides.  Pabbay was last inhabited in 1911.  The building was evidently constructed using the local stone, as it is quite well camouflaged against the bare rocks behind.  In the lower left, close to the photographer, is a standing stone, probably the remains of an ancient Celtic cross.",
          "alt": "Ruined Building on Pabbay, Outer Hebrides. This photo shows a ruined building on Pabbay, an island near Mingulay in the Outer Hebrides.  Pabbay was last inhabited in 1911.  The building was evidently constructed using the local stone, as it is quite well camouflaged against the bare rocks behind.  In the lower left, close to the photographer, is a standing stone, probably the remains of an ancient Celtic cross.",
